# CODEOWNERS — Blueprint instance (autonomous-factory two-layer routing)
#
# Layer model per ADR-issue-337-factory-phase-0-foundations.md (FR-011) and
# #339 Contract C6. Two routing layers:
#
#   Gate 1: Spec sign-off layer — maps the four canonical sign-off roles
#           (Product / Architecture / Security / Operations) to GitHub team
#           slugs. Each team is the corresponding `@sbonoc/factory-*` team
#           per Q-3 on specs/2026-05-28-issue-337-factory-phase-0-foundations/
#           spec.md, with at least 2 members each.
#
#   Gate 2: Bounded-context merge layer — per bounded context defined for
#           the blueprint repo (`factory`, `infra`, `docs`, `governance`
#           per Q-3), routing to the senior engineers responsible for that
#           context.
#
# The two-layer routing SHAPE is the #339 Contract C6 identical rule and
# applies to every consumer instance; only the per-instance team slugs
# below are parameterized via the #339 C8 consumer overlay.
#
# Existing AGENTS.md ownership boundaries (blueprint vs consumer vs
# platform code-ownership) are preserved — this file does NOT relax any
# of them; it adds GitHub-level review routing on top.
#
# Last-match-wins per GitHub's CODEOWNERS semantics: more specific globs
# below override the catch-all above. Order matters.


# ====================================================================
# Default catch-all
# ====================================================================
# Any file not matched by a more specific rule routes to the operations
# team. This is intentionally a wide net so nothing merges without
# explicit ownership routing.

*                                              @sbonoc/factory-operations


# ====================================================================
# === Gate 1: Spec sign-off layer ===
# ====================================================================
# Maps the four canonical sign-off roles to teams. Surfaces in this gate
# are the artifact types whose review is gated by the corresponding
# canonical sign-off phrase per AGENTS.md § Sign-off Policy.

# --- Product sign-off (SPEC_PRODUCT_READY: approved) ---
# Specs, intake artifacts, spec readiness gate, business-outcome rationale.
/specs/**/spec.md                              @sbonoc/factory-product
/specs/**/pr_context.md                        @sbonoc/factory-product
/specs/**/discovery.md                         @sbonoc/factory-product

# --- Architecture sign-off (ARCHITECTURE_SIGNOFF: approved) ---
# ADRs, design contracts, architecture artifacts.
/docs/blueprint/architecture/**                @sbonoc/factory-architecture
/docs/blueprint/autonomous-factory/design-contracts.md  @sbonoc/factory-architecture
/docs/blueprint/proposals/**                   @sbonoc/factory-architecture
/specs/**/architecture.md                      @sbonoc/factory-architecture
/specs/**/plan.md                              @sbonoc/factory-architecture
/specs/**/tasks.md                             @sbonoc/factory-architecture

# --- Security sign-off (SECURITY_SIGNOFF: approved) ---
# Security-sensitive surfaces: CODEOWNERS itself, sign-off policy, ESO/
# Secrets-Manager configs, NetworkPolicies, RBAC, IAM, factory bot
# identity, secret references, image-pull authentication.
/.github/CODEOWNERS                            @sbonoc/factory-security
/AGENTS.md                                     @sbonoc/factory-security @sbonoc/factory-architecture
/AGENTS.decisions.md                           @sbonoc/factory-security @sbonoc/factory-architecture
/blueprint/contract.yaml                       @sbonoc/factory-security @sbonoc/factory-architecture
/scripts/**/eso*.sh                            @sbonoc/factory-security
/scripts/**/secrets*.sh                        @sbonoc/factory-security
/scripts/**/networkpolicy*.sh                  @sbonoc/factory-security
/scripts/**/rbac*.sh                           @sbonoc/factory-security
/contracts/**                                  @sbonoc/factory-security @sbonoc/factory-architecture

# --- Operations sign-off (OPERATIONS_SIGNOFF: approved) ---
# CI/CD pipelines, observability config, runtime configs, factory runtime,
# instrumentation plan, baselines, on-call surfaces.
/.github/workflows/**                          @sbonoc/factory-operations
/.github/actions/**                            @sbonoc/factory-operations
/docs/blueprint/autonomous-factory/instrumentation-plan.md          @sbonoc/factory-operations
/docs/blueprint/autonomous-factory/pre-factory-baselines.md         @sbonoc/factory-operations
/docs/blueprint/autonomous-factory/triage-decomposition-data-feed.md @sbonoc/factory-operations
/Makefile                                      @sbonoc/factory-operations
/make/**                                       @sbonoc/factory-operations


# ====================================================================
# === Gate 2: Bounded-context merge layer ===
# ====================================================================
# Per bounded context: routes the merge-stage review to senior engineers
# in the relevant bounded-context team. Each team has ≥ 2 members per
# FR-011 (Operations verifies this at sign-off time).

# --- Bounded context: factory ---
# The autonomous-factory runtime, personas, skills, factory-specific
# ADRs and docs. NOTE: design-contracts.md routes to factory-architecture
# above (Gate 1) — it is co-owned by both gates because architectural
# sign-off is required AND bounded-context expertise is required.
/.agents/**                                    @sbonoc/factory-context-factory
/docs/blueprint/autonomous-factory/**          @sbonoc/factory-context-factory
/docs/blueprint/architecture/decisions/ADR-issue-33*  @sbonoc/factory-context-factory
/specs/*-issue-33*-factory-*                 @sbonoc/factory-context-factory

# --- Bounded context: infra ---
# Module wrappers, Terraform modules, Crossplane, ArgoCD, Helm, K8s
# manifests, infrastructure scripts.
/infra/**                                      @sbonoc/factory-context-infra
/scripts/templates/infra/**                    @sbonoc/factory-context-infra
/scripts/lib/infra/**                          @sbonoc/factory-context-infra
/scripts/bin/infra/**                          @sbonoc/factory-context-infra
/tests/infra/**                                @sbonoc/factory-context-infra
/apps/**                                       @sbonoc/factory-context-infra
/dags/**                                       @sbonoc/factory-context-infra

# --- Bounded context: docs ---
# All docs OUTSIDE of architecture decisions and autonomous-factory
# (those are factory-context). Includes blueprint-maintainer docs,
# platform docs, READMEs.
/docs/blueprint/**                             @sbonoc/factory-context-docs
/docs/platform/**                              @sbonoc/factory-context-docs
/README.md                                     @sbonoc/factory-context-docs

# --- Bounded context: governance ---
# SDD toolchain, AGENTS.md governance, lifecycle policies, sign-off
# policy, branch-naming, contract.yaml shape, .github/ITs, PR template,
# pre-commit hooks, anti-duplication contracts.
/AGENTS.backlog.md                             @sbonoc/factory-context-governance
/CLAUDE.md                                     @sbonoc/factory-context-governance
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/**                     @sbonoc/factory-context-governance
/.github/pull_request_template.md              @sbonoc/factory-context-governance
/.pre-commit-config.yaml                       @sbonoc/factory-context-governance
/scripts/lib/sdd/**                            @sbonoc/factory-context-governance
/scripts/lib/quality/**                        @sbonoc/factory-context-governance
/scripts/bin/sdd/**                            @sbonoc/factory-context-governance
/scripts/bin/quality/**                        @sbonoc/factory-context-governance
/tests/sdd/**                                  @sbonoc/factory-context-governance
/tests/blueprint/**                            @sbonoc/factory-context-governance


# ====================================================================
# Re-anchored gate-1 rules
# ====================================================================
# GitHub CODEOWNERS uses last-match-wins. Re-anchor the high-stakes
# gate-1 routings AFTER the bounded-context layer above so that
# CODEOWNERS itself, AGENTS.md, contract.yaml, and the factory workflow
# files preserve their gate-1 owners as the EFFECTIVE reviewers.

/.github/CODEOWNERS                            @sbonoc/factory-security
/AGENTS.md                                     @sbonoc/factory-security @sbonoc/factory-architecture
/AGENTS.decisions.md                           @sbonoc/factory-security @sbonoc/factory-architecture
/blueprint/contract.yaml                       @sbonoc/factory-security @sbonoc/factory-architecture
/.github/workflows/**                          @sbonoc/factory-operations
/.github/actions/**                            @sbonoc/factory-operations


# ====================================================================
# Re-anchored factory and architecture doc rules (defeat gate-2 docs catch-all)
# ====================================================================
# The broad `/docs/blueprint/**` rule above (Gate 2 docs section) would
# otherwise become the LAST match for architecture decisions and the
# autonomous-factory documents, sending high-stakes specs to the docs
# bounded-context team. Re-anchor the correct owners here so they remain
# the EFFECTIVE merge reviewers. Order matters within this block: broader
# patterns first, narrower patterns last.

# Gate-1 architecture for the architecture directory (broad)
/docs/blueprint/architecture/**                                        @sbonoc/factory-architecture

# Gate-1 architecture for strategic proposals targeting unpromoted/Draft
# epics. Re-anchored here so the broad /docs/blueprint/** docs-team rule
# above does NOT become the last match for proposal docs that are
# normative for future SDD intakes (per Codex P2 review on PR #377 —
# without this re-anchor, future edits to architecture-owned proposal
# docs would route to the docs-bounded-context team instead of the
# correct architecture reviewers).
/docs/blueprint/proposals/**                                           @sbonoc/factory-architecture

# Gate-2 factory bounded-context (narrower than architecture/** for ADRs;
# co-located with autonomous-factory docs). Factory ADRs CO-OWN architecture
# (gate-1) and factory-context-factory (gate-2) — both teams must be named
# on this final matching line so last-match-wins preserves architecture
# sign-off authority for factory ADRs (codex P2 round-11 — ADR ownership).
/.agents/**                                                            @sbonoc/factory-context-factory
/docs/blueprint/autonomous-factory/**                                  @sbonoc/factory-context-factory
/docs/blueprint/architecture/decisions/ADR-issue-33*                   @sbonoc/factory-context-factory @sbonoc/factory-architecture

# Gate-1 architecture for design-contracts.md (narrower than autonomous-factory/**).
# Co-owned with the gate-2 factory bounded-context team — both teams must be
# named on this final matching line so last-match-wins preserves the C6 / FR-011
# two-layer routing for the central factory design contract (codex P2 round-12
# — factory ownership on design contracts).
/docs/blueprint/autonomous-factory/design-contracts.md                 @sbonoc/factory-architecture @sbonoc/factory-context-factory

# Gate-1 operations for the three ops-owned factory documents
# (narrower than autonomous-factory/**, preserves FR-012/FR-014/FR-015
# operations sign-off authority). Co-owned with the gate-2 factory
# bounded-context team for the same C6 / FR-011 two-layer routing reason
# as design-contracts.md above.
/docs/blueprint/autonomous-factory/instrumentation-plan.md             @sbonoc/factory-operations @sbonoc/factory-context-factory
/docs/blueprint/autonomous-factory/pre-factory-baselines.md            @sbonoc/factory-operations @sbonoc/factory-context-factory
/docs/blueprint/autonomous-factory/triage-decomposition-data-feed.md   @sbonoc/factory-operations @sbonoc/factory-context-factory

# ====================================================================
# Re-anchored gate-1 spec routings for factory work items
# ====================================================================
# The Gate 2 rule `/specs/*-issue-33*-factory-*` above is the LAST match
# for factory work-item spec artifacts and would otherwise drop the
# gate-1 sign-off owners (Product on spec.md/pr_context.md/discovery.md;
# Architecture on architecture.md/plan.md/tasks.md). Re-anchor the gate-1
# teams on per-artifact narrower patterns AFTER the gate-2 line so the
# effective reviewer set includes BOTH the gate-1 sign-off owner AND the
# factory bounded-context team (codex P2 round-11 — Gate 1 owners on
# factory specs).

/specs/*-issue-33*-factory-*/spec.md                                 @sbonoc/factory-product @sbonoc/factory-context-factory
/specs/*-issue-33*-factory-*/pr_context.md                           @sbonoc/factory-product @sbonoc/factory-context-factory
/specs/*-issue-33*-factory-*/discovery.md                            @sbonoc/factory-product @sbonoc/factory-context-factory
/specs/*-issue-33*-factory-*/architecture.md                         @sbonoc/factory-architecture @sbonoc/factory-context-factory
/specs/*-issue-33*-factory-*/plan.md                                 @sbonoc/factory-architecture @sbonoc/factory-context-factory
/specs/*-issue-33*-factory-*/tasks.md                                @sbonoc/factory-architecture @sbonoc/factory-context-factory
